35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears our energy consumption is quite eclectic. Some rooms are essentially iceboxes requiring constant heating, while others are naturally cozy, leading to a significant disparity in actual power draw.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found out that calculating everything can be a real pain! Even with a template, you have to enter every single invoice, and some houses spend nearly an hour just logging readings and splitting totals.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The bills fluctuate quite a bit throughout the year. I also noticed some delays in our payment log, which suggests there might be some lingering confusion or disagreement about the amounts being asked.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"It seems that installing sub-meters would be quite expensive, both in initial costs and annual maintenance. Also, fixed payments can lead to waste if people stop being mindful of their usage.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I saw that some payments were really late, and it took a long time to decide what the new people should pay. It feels like we've had some trouble agreeing on the numbers before.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, it's fascinating that sub-meters are too pricey, as they would have solved the ""icebox"" problem. Without them, we're essentially asking the lucky south-room residents to subsidize the shivering of others.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, that sounds unfair, but if we try to be too precise, we might end up spending our whole evening doing math! I'm worried about who actually has to do the work.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, it seems we both noticed the payment delays. If people are questioning the amounts before paying, it suggests the current system doesn't feel equitable to everyone. We should address that tension.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, I agree. If the costs are unpredictable, it creates anxiety. However, we must be careful not to implement a system that is too complex to maintain or too expensive to start.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, thank you for noticing. I worry that when we argue about the numbers, it makes us feel bad toward each other. I don't like it when the house feels tense because of money.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I quite agree with Minato. There is a certain tragedy in wearing a winter coat indoors just to avoid a social conflict over a thermostat. We must be honest about the physical disparities of the rooms.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, you're so right about the complexity! If we make it too hard to maintain, the person in charge will just get burnt out. We need a way to be fair without it becoming a second job!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Mio. A system that is too demanding will only lead to more delays and frustration. Perhaps we can find a balance that acknowledges the room differences without requiring constant calculations.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, while the room disparities are real, we can't ignore the financial burden of fixing them. If we can't afford sub-meters, we need a predictable way to handle the winter spikes without it feeling like a second rent.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I think it's important that we all feel happy and safe here. If we can find a way to be fair that doesn't make us argue, maybe the house will feel more peaceful again.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are all in agreement that peace is preferable to precision. However, let us not mistake silence for fairness; a system that ignores the cold is merely a slow-burning fuse for future resentment.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I totally get that, Benjamin! But if we spend hours every month arguing over every single watt, we'll just be stressed in a different way. Let's find something that's ""fair enough"" and super quick to do!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I think we should prioritize a method that is transparent and consistent. If we can agree on a clear rule now, we can stop the cycle of questioning and delays that have plagued our payment log.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. Transparency is key to reducing anxiety. We need a solution that balances the physical differences of the rooms with a predictable cost structure, ensuring no one is blindsided by a massive bill in January.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,I hope we can choose something that makes everyone feel okay. I don't want anyone to feel like they are being accused of something just because of a bill. Let's be kind to each other.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
