60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option C is the only logically sound choice for fairness, as it eliminates the ""coat in February"" scenario. However, given Victoria's findings on the cost of sub-meters, I suspect it may be financially impractical.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is the fastest! No complicated templates or monthly math marathons. I'm really worried that if we pick something like C, someone's going to spend their whole Sunday doing paperwork!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option A is simple, but it doesn't address the underlying tension I saw in the payment logs. If people already feel they are carrying others, a flat split might just continue that cycle of resentment.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option C is far too expensive to implement, as the installation and maintenance costs are prohibitive. Option A is simple, but it doesn't solve the problem of unpredictable winter spikes that can feel like a second rent.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think Option A is very easy, but Jonathan is right that it might not stop the arguments. I'm worried that if we don't feel it's fair, we might start feeling bad toward each other again.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, while I admire your quest for efficiency, ""fast"" is not a synonym for ""fair."" If we choose Option A, we are simply agreeing to ignore the fact that some of us are freezing while others are basking.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I know it's not perfect, but ""fair"" doesn't help if the person managing the bills is too stressed to function! Option B could be a great middle ground—predictable and way less work than C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, I think Option B is a strong alternative. It provides the predictability Victoria wants and avoids the administrative burden you're worried about, while still being more stable than a flat monthly split.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, I agree. Option B allows us to budget for the cold months in advance, which removes the shock of a sudden spike. It provides the stability I'm looking for without the impossible cost of Option C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Mio, Option B sounds like a good idea. If we know the amount ahead of time, maybe we won't have to ask each other for money so often, and that might make things feel more peaceful.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B is certainly a more elegant compromise than A. While it doesn't solve the thermal injustice of the rooms, it at least prevents the financial shock that often triggers those unpleasant house meetings.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm so glad we're on the same page! Option B sounds like a win-win. It's predictable for Victoria and Minato, and it won't turn into a nightmare of spreadsheets for whoever handles the money!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. Option B creates a consistent expectation for everyone, which should stop the cycle of questioning and late payments. It's a gentle way to maintain harmony while keeping the administration simple.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I'm satisfied with Option B. It addresses my need for financial predictability and avoids the prohibitive costs of sub-meters, all while remaining manageable for the house. It's the most rational balance for us.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm happy that we all agree. If we can just follow a simple rule together, I think we can stop worrying about the money and just enjoy being friends in the house. I'll vote for B!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Since we have collectively decided that peace and predictability outweigh the desire for absolute precision, I shall concede. I'll vote for Option B, provided we promise to be honest about the cold.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm totally in for B! It's the perfect way to keep things fair and friendly without making anyone's life a living nightmare of math. I'm voting for Option B!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I'll vote for Option B as well. It seems the most effective way to ensure a quiet, harmonious atmosphere and put an end to the payment disputes.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I will also vote for Option B. It is the only choice that provides the necessary financial stability and predictability without imposing an unreasonable cost or administrative burden on any of us.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm voting for Option B too. I'm really glad we could decide this together without any fighting. Let's all be kind to each other from now on!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
